# What `docker build` must NEVER copy into an image layer.
#
# This file is load-bearing, not housekeeping. The Dockerfile ends with `COPY . .`,
# and `backend/.env` holds PINECONE_API_KEY, NVIDIA_API_KEY and all three
# clearance keys. Without this file those values get baked into a layer, and an
# image layer is a distributable artifact: anyone who can pull the image can read
# them back out with `docker history` or by extracting the layer. Nothing about a
# later `docker run --env-file` undoes it — the secret is already in the image.
#
# That would quietly defeat the entire point of the auth work. RAG_KEY_EXECUTIVE
# *is* the security boundary; a boundary that ships inside the build output is not
# one. Runtime env only: see docker-compose.prod.yml and deploy/GO_LIVE.md.

# --- Secrets -----------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key

# --- Local state that must not become image content -------------------------
# Baking a dev audit.db in would ship one tenant's query history to every
# deployment, and uploads/ can hold whatever anyone dropped on a local test.
data/
uploads/
*.db
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3

# --- Build/dev cruft ---------------------------------------------------------
venv/
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
tests/__pycache__/

# --- Not needed at runtime ---------------------------------------------------
.git/
.gitignore
.DS_Store
*.log
eval_report.json
